  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Supporting Justice Sector Reform &#x2013; Phase VI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To advance institutional capacities of the Office of the Prosecutor General                (OPG) in line with the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) standards and organizational reform                priorities. 2) To strengthen institutional and professional capacities of anti-corruption and law                enforcement bodies. 3) To strengthen independence and improve efficiency of Ukraine&#x2019;s judicial                administration. 4) To increase transparency of the reform implementation. 5) To enhance capacity of                public institutions to implement public sector, anti-corruption and governance reforms. 6) To enhance                legal basis and strategic foundations for criminal justice and public policy reform initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Office of the Prosecutor General (OPG), Training Centre of                Prosecutors of Ukraine (TCPU), National Anti-Corruption Bureau (NABU), Specialized Anti-corruption                Prosecutor&#x2019;s Office (SAPO), line ministries and agencies of the Government of Ukraine (GoU),                Regional State Administrations and local self-governing bodies, anti-corruption civil society                organizations. Indirect beneficiaries: Ukrainian population at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to advance rule of law and public sector reforms in Ukraine by                strengthening the integrity, efficiency and transparency of the criminal justice and improving legal and                regulatory regimes in criminal justice and public sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
